Package: dapcb
Type: Package
Title: Design-Aware Population Conformal Bands
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("The", "Authors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "anonymized@review.invalid",
    comment = "Anonymized while the companion paper is under review")
Description: Finite-sample simultaneous conformal bands for whole trajectories
    of population-level curves (e.g. a country's attitude CDF across survey
    waves), with the population as the exchangeable unit. Implements the
    nominal-safe adaptive selector of the companion paper "The Wrong Unit of
    Uncertainty": a clustered population conformal band that is exact at any
    number of calibration populations, inside a selection-free selector that
    activates a design-noise deconvolution only where four target-blind gates
    certify it is reliable, and otherwise falls back to the exact clustered
    band or a conservative envelope. A pure-R port of the reference Python
    implementation; numerical agreement is enforced by golden tests generated
    from the Python package.
